
<p>From the NetNewsWire blog:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>The <a href="https://netnewswire.blog/2026/10/16/netnewswire-for-ios-unread-count.html">latest version</a> of NetNewsWire for iOS supports iPhone
Duo, which is very much a novel iPhone with toolbars running up
the side and all kinds of behavior.</p>

<p>How we did it: we didn’t do any work at all. We built the app
using Xcode 27.1 and the default iOS SDK that comes with it, and
that’s it.</p>

<p>Here’s the thing, though: we were already using standard controls — toolbars, navigation controllers, split views, etc. — and we
were paying attention to size classes and such (as opposed to just
looking at device type).</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Develop your app the right way and, depending on the app, it might literally be no work at all to produce a great version for the Duo. Develop your app the wrong way and it might take months. NetNewsWire is one of my most-used apps. I keep it in my home screen dock, alongside Messages, Notes, and Safari. It would drive me nuts to use a Duo without a version of NetNewsWire that adapts to the Duo’s novel display sizes.</p>

